# Create / move / delete an operator (user) waypoint. One op-dispatched service,
# one handler. Operator waypoints live in a separate store from the auto/geometry
# anchors; auto/frontier waypoints cannot be moved or deleted (relabel the region
# instead). There is no per-pin name in v1 (the published WayPoint.msg has no name
# field and nothing in the UI shows one).
string op        # "add" | "move" | "delete"
uint32 id        # move/delete target; ignored for add (server assigns)
float64 x        # add/move (map frame, meters)
float64 y
float64 yaw      # add/move
bool has_yaw     # if false, server derives a default (face place peak, else 0)
---
bool success
string message   # rejection reason on failure (e.g. "too close to a wall/obstacle")
uint32 id        # created/affected waypoint id
